    "checks/independent/dfm-continuum-interface.py": {
      "role": "Bounded finite SL2 connection verification application with owned immutable labels, typed signed/fixed-graph transport, rooted dressing and dependency controls",
      "origin": "lean4/DressingFieldContinuumInterface.lean",
      "profile": "Exact",
      "cost": "Connection<=4096 named labels, each1..64 characters and exact integer2x2 determinant-one matrix. Signed/fixed-graph paths<=4096 steps. Admission and transport are O(labels+steps) fixed2x2 operations with4096-bit stored entries and product/dot/determinant budgets. Conservative intermediate refusal may reject a mathematically valid large SL2 matrix or product. Fixed-graph dressing uses the supplied paths of length<=2. Additive inputs/outputs<=4096 bits. Default511 executed obligations,85 loop words and255 append cases. Path-law fixture prefixes<=4095 to reserve one suffix step.",
      "groups": [
        {
          "requirement": "Validate nonempty bounded edge names, fixed-graph membership and exact integer2x2 determinant-one matrices before algebra. Reject bool/float/symbolic/fractional entries, oversized arithmetic and determinant-1 matrices. Export detached immutable SymPy matrices while using the reviewed rational matrix value internally.",
